; The platform. Geometry, ray casting, rendering, SDL — everything a frame is
; actually made of, and none of it anything a game should have to name.
;
; It is called core for the reason the directory is: what a game opens is the
; layer over the top, and this is what that layer is over. A game that
; genuinely needs World or Renderer adds camlcast.core to its own dune
; explicitly, so crossing the boundary is a decision rather than a drift.

; -w +70 is "every module in here has an .mli", which every module in here
; already has: the flag costs nothing and keeps it that way. A module without an
; interface exports every binding in it, so the boundary this library draws
; would be whatever its implementation happens to leave visible. Set per library
; rather than at the root, because demo/ is deliberately .mli-less, one showcase
; per file.

(library
 (flags
  (:standard -w +70))
 (name camlcast_core)
 (public_name camlcast.core)
 (libraries tsdl tsdl-image))
